# Accounting / Financial Module — Technical Audit Plan

**Repository:** `posnew` (monorepo)  
**Stack:** `apps/pos-backend` (Express, Mongoose, MongoDB), `apps/pos-frontend2` (Next.js Studio), `apps/saas-dash` (platform operator — separate from tenant GL)  
**Audit method:** Static code and route review (2026-04-21). No production DB sampling or browser E2E in this pass.

---

## Legend (per your requested format)

| Badge | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| ✅ | Fully implemented (end-to-end for typical use) |
| ⚠ | Partially implemented, config-dependent, beta, or integrity caveats |
| ❌ | Missing |
| 🔴 | Broken or high-risk incorrect behavior |
| 🔗 | Not connected (schema/API/UI/doc drift, dead field, API without UI, etc.) |

For each flagged item: **path → function/component → problem → recommended fix.**

---

## 1. Core accounting features

| Feature | Status | Notes |
|---------|--------|--------|
| Chart of accounts | ✅ | `accountingAccountModel.js`, `GET/POST/PATCH /api/accounting/accounts`, Studio `/dashboard/accounting/accounts` |
| General ledger | ✅ | Aggregate of `JournalEntry` lines; account drill-down `GET /api/accounting/accounts/:id/ledger` |
| Journal entries | ✅ | `journalEntryModel.js`, `POST /api/accounting/journal-entries` (manual), auto sources |
| Double-entry accounting | ✅ | `journalEntrySchema.pre("validate")` enforces debits = credits, no debit+credit on same line |
| Accounts receivable | ⚠ | Invoices + `Customer.arBalance` + on-account orders; no dedicated “supplier-style” subledger for all AR sources in one place |
| Accounts payable | ⚠ | `VendorBill` + GL postings; **no** `apBalance` on `supplierModel.js` |
| Customer balances | ✅ | `customerModel.js` `arBalance`, `unappliedCredit`; `postArPayment` in `accountingService.js` |
| Supplier balances | ⚠ | Derived from `vendorBillModel` (`total`, `amountPaid`, `status`); not a single balance field on supplier |
| Income tracking | ✅ | Revenue accounts + P&amp;L + POS sale journals |
| Expense tracking | ⚠ | **Expense reports** module (`ExpenseReport` + Studio) posts to GL; broader policy/approval workflows still org-dependent |
| Tax handling | ✅ | Order `bills.tax`, config tax maps, sale journal metadata |
| VAT handling | ⚠ | Same as tax (VAT is operational naming); mapping in `AccountingConfig` tax rate rows |
| Discounts | ✅ | Staff/loyalty discounts in `postOrderSaleLedger`; `defaultDiscountAccount` |
| Payment methods | ✅ | `paymentMethodAccounts` on config; `resolveTenderAccount` pattern in service |
| Cash register balancing | ✅ | `AccountingSession`, open/close routes, `session_close` journals |
| Bank accounts | ⚠ | GL cash/clearing accounts + **bank statement lines** (import/match), not multi-bank master data |
| Bank reconciliation | ⚠ | CSV import, match, reconciliation report — labeled **beta** in navigation (`sidebar-items.ts`) |
| Multi-currency support | ⚠ | `documentCurrency`, `fxRateToCompany`, `fxRateModel`; FX resolve endpoints |
| Financial periods | ✅ | `accountingPeriodModel`, list/close, posting guard `assertPostingAllowedForDate` |
| Closing periods | ✅ | `POST /api/accounting/periods/close` + retained earnings closing route |
| Trial balance | ✅ | `GET /api/accounting/trial-balance`, exports PDF/XLSX |
| Profit &amp; loss | ✅ | `GET /api/accounting/reports/pnl`, Studio page |
| Balance sheet | ✅ | `GET /api/accounting/reports/balance-sheet` |
| Cash flow statement | ✅ | `GET /api/accounting/reports/cash-flow` |
| Cost centers | ⚠ | **Analytics:** `journalEntry` line `analytics.costCenter` + bill propagation; TB/PnL/BS/cash-flow optional `costCenter` filter — not full allocation engine |
| Branch accounting | ⚠ | **Analytics:** `analytics.branchId` / `locationId` from orders; entry-level `location` unchanged — no eliminations |
| Audit trail | ⚠ | `journalAuditLogModel.js` + `listAuditLogs`; journals themselves are not updated in app code (immutability by design) |

### Issues (core)

- ⚠ **Auto-post vs paid order** — `apps/pos-backend/services/accountingService.js` → `onOrderBecamePaid` — Catches `postOrderSaleLedger` failures and sets `accountingSaleStatus: "failed"` on order; order can still be **paid** without successful sale journal when misconfigured. **Fix:** Optional strict mode (fail PATCH paid), or queue/retry + alerting (see `SYSTEM_AUDIT_MASTER.md`).
- ⚠ **Period close vs reality** — Same file → `assertPostingAllowedForDate` — Depends on periods existing/maintained per org; edge cases if periods not seeded. **Fix:** Bootstrap periods on org create; admin warning in Studio.

