## 4. Database connections

**Engine:** MongoDB via Mongoose — **no** SQL triggers or stored procedures (by design).

| Topic | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|--------|
| Accounting-related collections | ✅ | Accounts, journals, config, periods, sessions, invoices, vendor bills, expense reports, approvals, FX, budgets, bank lines, credit notes, gift cards, audit log |
| Foreign keys | ⚠ | Logical refs (`ObjectId` + populate); **no** DB-level referential enforcement |
| Missing links | ✅ | Vendor bill → posted journal id **resolved (2026-04-21)** |
| Duplicate logic | ⚠ | Tender resolution appears in multiple flows (orders, AP payment) — maintain one helper (partially already `resolveTenderAccount`) |
| Orphaned financial records | ⚠ | Possible if orders/customers deleted without cascade policy — not fully audited here |

### Issues (DB)

- ❌ **Mongo triggers / RPC** — N/A for this stack. **Fix:** N/A; use app services + idempotency keys (already on `JournalEntry`).

